1
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten up the peace,
then step away and see.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:32,680
I walked looking back.

4
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:35,340
Led by the hand by Gā-chan,

5
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,280
that strange feeling I had back then.

6
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,740
So the tiles of the arcade street

7
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black ones.

8
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,700
Everyone was a child once,

9
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

10
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,820
Politicians with their haughty faces,

11
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:09,120
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

12
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:12,120
Try turning the corner.

13
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,700
That corner.

14
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

15
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:24,520
Over there is Kame-ari.

16
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:27,820
Surely there is Kame-ari.

17
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:33,040
Everyone, come to our town.

18
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:34,620
Thank you.

19
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,980
Muscle-type magic practitioner.

20
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:46,980
I'm home.

21
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,100
Welcome back.

22
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:53,000
Hey, I got a prize from the
shopping district lottery.

23
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,600
I won this.

24
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:59,580
"Hiel Nishikawaguchi"?
Sounds like an apartment building name.

25
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:01,440
This smells fishy.

26
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:05,880
You don't know him, senpai?
He's the talk of the town right now!

27
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:06,260
This guy?

28
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,780
He's walked through the Berlin Wall
and the top of the Great Wall of China,

29
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:13,980
strolled around on the
wings of a flying jet,

30
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:18,040
and lived for a month in
a box buried underground.

31
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,340
He's Magic-chan,
famous for his grand-scale magic tricks.

32
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:25,220
That's amazing, he's like Superman!

33
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:29,640
What are you talking about? It's magic,
so of course there's a trick to it!

34
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,780
But I hear it's quite a spectacle.

35
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,560
Let's all go see it on our next day off.

36
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,640
Doesn't that sound fun, Yacchan?

37
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,100
I suppose I'll go watch it for the story.

38
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:19,460
Thank you for your hard work.

39
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,240
Welcome!

40
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:24,060
Welcome, everyone.

41
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:28,540
I am Pierre Nishikawaguchi,
a licensed magician.

42
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:33,160
Amazing! How on earth did he do that?

43
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,920
Coming out of such a small box!

44
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,880
Don't be so amazed by that much.

45
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:43,780
There should be a trapdoor on
this stage for stage effects.

46
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:44,780
A trapdoor?

47
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:49,760
So if he opens the bottom of that
box and rises up through the hole,

48
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,860
Welcome!

49
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:52,460
I see.

50
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,900
Using such a childish trick.

51
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:58,360
A licensed magician, my foot.
It's appalling.

52
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:01,300
With this, I'm worried about
how the rest of the show will go.

53
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,400
They say the first part is hypnosis.

54
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:08,060
Is there anyone who would be
willing to help with the hypnosis?

55
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:11,720
Yes, yes, yes, I'll volunteer!

56
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,280
Alright, then you, sir.

57
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,180
Hey, I raised my hand first, you bastard!

58
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:17,360
Hey, hey!

59
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,620
Senpai!

60
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:21,220
Okay, you're getting sleepier and sleepier.

61
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,400
Getting sleepy...

62
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,340
Now, when I count to three,

63
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,780
you'll become a rabbit.

64
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:29,920
One, two...

65
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:30,780
*Swish*

66
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:35,060
*Hop, hop, hop, hop*

67
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,840
You are Takashi Fujii!

68
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:39,420
Hah, hah, hah, hah!

69
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:40,080
No, that's wrong.

70
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,080
You're completely under, aren't you?

71
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,020
And that man over there is a plant.

72
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,160
Your voice is too loud.

73
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:52,500
If you pick the plant you planted in the audience,
you can make him a rabbit or anything else you like.

74
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,240
Since you control it completely,
it's a classic technique.

75
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:01,100
Now, please, this gentleman too,
come up on stage.

76
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:05,260
What an interesting show!
Go on, hypnotize me.

77
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:07,580
You're getting sleepier and sleepier.

78
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:10,200
Sleepier.

79
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,280
I don't feel anything at all!

80
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,720
Ryo-chan, you're being so defiant.

81
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,760
I just hope it doesn't turn into a fight.

82
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,540
There, you're getting sleepy...

83
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:22,080
Far from it,
I'm getting more and more wide awake.

84
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:26,500
As you grow sleepier, I'll give you money.

85
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:29,300
Yes.

86
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,520
Even Senpai's been hypnotized!

87
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,560
So it really is the real thing after all.

88
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,920
Now, you're a little sparrow!

89
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:42,500
Now, let's soar across the big open sky.

90
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,980
How much is it?

91
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:50,840
1,000 yen

92
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,440
I woke up.

93
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,960
What the hell is this?

94
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,340
Why did you wake me up?

95
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:57,360
Figures, it's just a sham.

96
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:02,400
I'll give it another try,

97
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,900
you're getting sleepier and sleepier.

98
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,680
Getting sleepy.

99
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,320
You're getting more and more...

100
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,140
3,000 yen

101
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:10,900
10,000 yen

102
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:11,960
Getting sleepy.

103
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,820
5,000 yen

104
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:13,560
10,000 yen

105
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:17,960
Getting sleepy.

106
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,020
Got it, waves hand.

107
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,460
Yes, you're a dog. You become a dog.

108
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:31,420
Yes, you can't help but want
to dance the Chichikuri Mambo.

109
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:35,180
Chichikuri Mambo, Chichikuri Mambo,
squeak-squeak with the Chichikuri Mambo!

110
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:37,260
Okay, next up is Konto 55!

111
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:38,480
I'm flying, I'm flying.

112
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,420
Bye.

113
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:46,560
Ryo-chan of all people turning into that.

114
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,800
And I didn't believe it at all.

115
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:51,200
Well, he's completely hooked.

116
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,520
That guy's the real thing.

117
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,120
The second part is about to begin.

118
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,320
That was pretty amazing, wasn't it?

119
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,740
I've got some business to attend to,

120
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,680
so you two go on home first.

121
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:17,600
What are you talking about?

122
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,680
What do you mean? I'm here to collect
the 10,000 yen you promised me earlier.

123
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:24,120
What a simple-minded man.

124
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:27,180
That conversation was the hypnosis spell,
you see.

125
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:31,200
So you fell perfectly under my hypnosis.

126
00:07:31,650 --> 00:07:33,200
That's cheating, you bastard!

127
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,500
3,000 yen, 5,000 yen, 10,000 yen!

128
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,460
There's no way I'd act like that!

129
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:38,440
Quit your blabbering

130
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,900
and hand over the money, you bastard!

131
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,520
Alright, alright.

132
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,860
Don't be an idiot,
just hand it over honestly like that.

133
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:49,920
You made me go to all this extra trouble,
you bastard.

134
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,600
What the hell is this?

135
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,140
It's just a scrap of paper!

136
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:00,020
I'm the real deal, the real me.

137
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:02,220
Don't use magic, you bastard!

138
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:06,660
I told you not to use magic, damn it!

139
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,760
Yeah, yeah, yeah...

140
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:11,800
Seriously,
I told you to stop with the magic already!

141
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,800
You little runt!

142
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,200
If it comes to this,
I'll tell everyone your hypnosis is a fake.

143
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,680
I'll spread it around to everyone!

144
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,780
What is this?

145
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:33,460
If you calm down and back off,
I could take them off for you.

146
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:35,140
Otherwise...

147
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:39,160
I might just send this key
to my grandma in Siberia.

148
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:40,100
What?

149
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:44,300
Grandma, take care of it.

150
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:46,380
What are we supposed to do with this?

151
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:48,880
Will it come off?

152
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:50,220
It's suffocating!

153
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,740
You bastard!

154
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,300
Who needs a key?

155
00:08:54,580 --> 00:09:16,700
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm

156
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,580
I'm serious.
Of course I'll pay your monthly salary.

157
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:22,375
What are you talking about?
After working me to the bone,

158
00:09:22,425 --> 00:09:25,260
you're going to say it's another hypnosis spell,
aren't you?

159
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:26,980
Pay up, damn it.

160
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,000
It'll just be blank paper again, won't it?

161
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:34,196
No, no.
This time it's the real thing, I swear.

162
00:09:34,246 --> 00:09:35,780
See? How about it?

163
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:40,620
Hey, isn't that Ryo-chan? Look, that guy.

164
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:43,360
No matter how you look at it,
that's our senior.

165
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:48,160
Figures. He called in saying he had a bad cold,
but it was a fake illness after all.

166
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:51,820
And now, the climax of the magic show!

167
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:56,060
Pierre Nishikawaguchi and the
strongman Mogambo from Brazil

168
00:09:56,060 --> 00:10:00,920
will perform the miraculous grand illusion of
passing through a wall once used as a prison wall.

169
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,020
We bring it to you live.

170
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,440
Let's try a quick interview.

171
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:14,300
Mr. P, you're attempting it live. Any words?

172
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:18,580
He appears to be concentrating.

173
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:23,280
Now, Mogambo-san, any words?

174
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:24,200
Mogambo!

175
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:27,900
Let's watch this miraculous moment.

176
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:33,040
Will it succeed?

177
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:36,020
Hey.

178
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,540
Aaaaaah!

179
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,640
After this,

180
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:50,900
What is it?

181
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,160
Yes, you're helping too.

182
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,120
Quick!

183
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:59,400
I was once in a Ranger unit, you know.

184
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,660
What an impressive past.

185
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,420
Well then, let's open the curtain.

186
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:04,240
Well?

187
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,120
Couldn't they just dig a tunnel beforehand?

188
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,820
That's totally a con, isn't it?

189
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:10,940
It's still just magic, damn it.

190
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:14,580
By the way, I hear you walk
on the wings of flying planes.

191
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,980
What's the trick behind that?

192
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:18,680
That's my miracle power, pure and simple.

193
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:20,440
Don't put on airs now.

194
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:24,000
I'm wearing shoes with
powerful suction cups.

195
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,040
That's it?

196
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:26,980
Every time,
it was a matter of life and death.

197
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:30,300
So you'd stay in a box
underground for a month

198
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:31,420
That's

199
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,560
Don't say it! I'll guess it myself!

200
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:36,340
they dig a tunnel beforehand,
come out of it,

201
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:37,740
hide somewhere,

202
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:40,880
then get back inside the
box when it's tossed up.

203
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,200
Exactly.

204
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:46,460
They hid in the forest so they wouldn't
run into anyone while they were in hiding.

205
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,860
It must have been lonely, all by themselves.

206
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:51,940
Just imagining it,
it's pretty dull and dreary.

207
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:54,860
To create miracles that look
illogical to the audience,

208
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:57,620
day and night, endless research and effort.

209
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:01,040
Magicians piece together steady,
rational work.

210
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,900
Once a magician starts talking about his hardships,
it's all over.

211
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,200
Anyway, are we running out of time?

212
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,180
Oh no!

213
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,880
Now it's time for the miracle moment!

214
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:15,540
3, 2, 1, open!

215
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,220
That was truly splendid.

216
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,380
Excuse me.

217
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:28,460
We've had viewer comments asking to see
you pass through without using a curtain.

218
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:29,380
Yes, that's right.

219
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:31,960
Please,
let us see that scene right in front of us.

220
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:34,200
Do it without the curtain!

221
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,560
You're not just digging a hole in the ground,
are you?

222
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,320
I heard that.

223
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:39,440
PL

224
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:41,920
PL

225
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:43,820
PL

226
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:44,740
PL

227
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:01,620
How much is it?

228
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:02,820
Which one?

229
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,360
If it's this wall,

230
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,260
Alright, 3,000 yen.

231
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:07,040
20,000.

232
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,820
5,000.

233
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:08,900
20,000.

234
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,000
That's too expensive!

235
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:11,360
Something else?

236
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:16,740
No, if Mogambo, the girl,
does the wall-passing trick in my place,

237
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,000
Is that really true?

238
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,000
This is going to be amazing.

239
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,500
We're going to perform the human
wall-passing without a curtain!

240
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:24,780
10,000 yen

241
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:25,500
20,000 yen

242
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,820
A never-before-seen, unprecedented,
once-in-all-of-history grand magic!

243
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:29,260
Human wall-passing!

244
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:32,460
We would like to bring you the
curtain-less version once again!

245
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:41,160
Now, in place of my master,
Pierre Nishikawaguchi, I will...

246
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:44,080
We will now perform the wall-passing trick!

247
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,420
Will Ryotsu really be able
to pass through the wall?

248
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,320
The result will come in 90 seconds.

249
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,180
Eloim essaim, eloim essaim.

250
00:14:12,180 --> 00:14:16,660
Ton-hira-koppe-dobita-bujo,
tamore, tamore, kabe-nukete, tamore!

251
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,140
Yaaah!

252
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,720
W-what is this...

253
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,720
He just passed through the wall...
uh the wall-passing's gonna tear off!

254
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,940
That's how it works: by twisting like that,
he gradually merges into the wall.

255
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,580
And he came right through it.

256
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:00,420
As you saw,
he passed right through the wall.

257
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:02,780
Once you get used to it,
passing through becomes even smoother.

258
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:05,760
Amazing! Just incredible!
It's like a miracle!

259
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:08,420
He made it through!
Mogambo passed through the wall!

260
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:12,200
Yes! With this, we can get 30%!

261
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,460
What incredible brute strength!

262
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,540
For a second,
I really thought he had passed through.

263
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,660
But is this really magic?

264
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,760
It's small.

265
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:33,440
It's ridiculous that the apprentice is
being treated better than the master.

266
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:37,940
Of course I'm the one who's bigger, since
I'm the one putting my body on the line.

267
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:39,060
But you see,

268
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,140
just so you know,

269
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:44,600
I never intended to become your disciple,
not even a little.

270
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:48,280
I just call myself your disciple for convenience,
because it's quicker that way.

271
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:52,580
David Copperfield made the
Statue of Liberty disappear again?

272
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:53,220
What?

273
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,600
The spaced-out Kappa played the flute?

274
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:59,660
You're a magician and you don't
even know David Copperfield?

275
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:02,100
Flying through the sky,
making trains vanish,

276
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:06,220
he's a top-class magician and a world billionaire,
in name and in reality.

277
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:06,780
What?

278
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:10,200
Yes~

279
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:13,340
I'm flying even more than usual.

280
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:16,940
Yes~

281
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:17,760
Curse you!

282
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:20,380
How dare that kappa be so cocky!

283
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,441
You two pulled off a magnificent
wall-passing trick the other day,

284
00:16:26,491 --> 00:16:29,640
so what kind of magic are
you planning to attempt next?

285
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,280
Well, that's...

286
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:31,700
Urgh!

287
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,031
My rival,

288
00:16:33,081 --> 00:16:36,221
if that radio-wave kappa made
the Statue of Liberty vanish,

289
00:16:36,271 --> 00:16:39,800
I'll have the Great Buddha
of Nara make a peace sign!

290
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:45,610
Then, Miracle Magic Pierre Power,

291
00:16:45,660 --> 00:16:49,460
Miracle cool cool cool, peace peace!

292
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,680
What's with the peace sign?
Showing off all by yourself!

293
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:12,760
Mr. Pierre,
what kind of magic will you attempt next?

294
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:17,400
Because my rival, the Denpa Kappa,
flew over the Grand Canyon.

295
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:21,480
I will become the wind
of the Tottori Sand Dunes.

296
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:26,120
That's not magic or anything like it!

297
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,560
Well, well.

298
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:35,940
This is something that won't
lose even to the Teppo Kappa.

299
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,180
Pierre Nishikawaguchi's miracle magic!

300
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:46,260
If that's how it is,
then do it yourself, I'm telling you.

301
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,840
Okay, spin around, spin around!

302
00:17:49,880 --> 00:18:16,100
Nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn...

303
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:18,200
No matter how much special pay we get,

304
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,100
it just doesn't suit me.

305
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,580
Nothing matters more than staying alive,
you know.

306
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,260
I'm quitting.

307
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:23,260
Come on...

308
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,920
We're finally starting to get popular!

309
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:29,020
Plus, they just confirmed
a two-hour special on CX.

310
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:30,720
So let's keep working together,
the two of us,

311
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:32,360
and push through to the end.

312
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,460
I'm the only one putting my body on the line here,
damn it!

313
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:35,500
Yeah, right.

314
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:38,940
Anyway, I'm going back to my
real job as a police officer.

315
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:40,680
Pay me all my hazard pay

316
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,760
and settle up.

317
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,480
All in cash, got it?

318
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,960
Don't say that.

319
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,840
Absolutely?

320
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,180
Absolutely.

321
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:52,080
Fine! Then this is my last request.

322
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:54,180
It's Mogambo's retirement
grand escape, so...

323
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:56,740
Just one more,
just one more job, please take it.

324
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,580
I'll pay you ten times your usual fee,
so come on.

325
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:00,800
A hundred times!

326
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:03,080
Deal.

327
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,600
It's starting, Reiko-san.

328
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:09,160
Looks like even Ryo-chan's
body can't take it anymore.

329
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,080
Yeah.

330
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:14,920
Hello, everyone!

331
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:18,017
Japan's proud number one magician,

332
00:19:18,067 --> 00:19:23,740
the day has come to bring you the miraculous grand escape by Pierre Nishikawaguchi and his apprentice duo,
Mogambo!

333
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:27,871
Unfortunately, Mogambo-san is
retiring after this performance,

334
00:19:27,921 --> 00:19:30,400
and will be returning
to his homeland, Brazil!

335
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:34,400
Pierre-san, this escape seems to be
more large-scale than ever before!

336
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:38,090
That's right. First, at the starting point,

337
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:42,480
the box containing Mogambo, with his hands
and feet tied, will suddenly be blown up.

338
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,440
Right at the start?

339
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:50,680
Then, having narrowly escaped,
Mogambo runs into this tunnel.

340
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:55,420
But inside this tunnel,
all sorts of traps are waiting for him.

341
00:19:55,420 --> 00:20:02,280
And if Mogambo makes it to the goal, he
can take home the prize of one million yen.

342
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:03,880
I see.

343
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:06,280
Right, and that's not all.

344
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:10,740
If he doesn't press this button at the goal
within the five-minute escape time limit,

345
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:14,160
a massive explosion will occur at the goal.

346
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:15,440
A massive explosion?

347
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:18,060
This looks like it's
going to be something big.

348
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:26,740
Just you wait, 1 million yen!

349
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:30,140
Can he really escape when
he's tied up so tightly?

350
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:34,620
I hear these magic acts are
designed with proper safety measures.

351
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:36,800
Once the magic has begun,

352
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:40,900
I've heard the performer has
already evacuated to a safe place.

353
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:41,620
Right?

354
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,660
And now, we're finally starting!

355
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:45,800
Look forward to an
unprecedented great escape!

356
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,240
Ready, set, go!

357
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,860
The starting point has just been blown up!

358
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:55,960
Is Mogambo really safe?

359
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,260
1 million yen, 1 million yen!

360
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,640
There's Mogambo now!

361
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,620
Looks like he's okay.

362
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,580
Something's slippery, slippery!

363
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:29,600
As expected of Mogambo. Impressive work.

364
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,060
We're only just getting started.

365
00:21:41,640 --> 00:22:03,900
!
Translation>
!

366
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,800
Don't look, don't look, don't look!

367
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,160
The baby is sleeping.

368
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,360
One million yen, one million yen!

369
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:20,080
Move aside!

370
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:30,600
What the heck is this?

371
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:38,940
Are you going, sir?

372
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:46,920
I knew something like this might happen, so I hid
a low-frequency underwear measuring device on me.

373
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:58,500
Aw, what a shame, so close!

374
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:02,160
My million, my million!

375
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:04,700
What is this?

376
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:07,780
Hey, what's this toy money?

377
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:10,640
No, the show was a huge success!

378
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,300
They're even talking
about making it a series.

379
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:14,780
Let's do one more together.

380
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,580
Don't mess around, pay me my cut properly!

381
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:19,040
I don't have any money.

382
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:22,680
Don't lie! You must have the money
we've been earning together all this time.

383
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:25,600
I poured everything into this escape.

384
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,360
Not a single yen is left.

385
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,360
You dirty bastard!

386
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,520
No money, so no money, nyah!

387
00:23:32,740 --> 00:23:33,580
Help!

388
00:23:34,060 --> 00:23:35,880
My pay up to now,

389
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:38,900
because now you're going
to earn big for me, got it?

390
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:41,100
For the first time ever,

391
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:45,180
a miraculous escape from
a Tomahawk in flight!

392
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:46,820
Launch is imminent.

393
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:47,580
Help me!

394
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:57,900
No way, I can't escape!

395
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:05,220
What's going on?

396
00:24:05,220 --> 00:24:07,660
Komachi suddenly became a star.

397
00:24:07,660 --> 00:24:09,740
Wherever you look, left or right,

398
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:11,560
it's a Komachi-Komachi craze!

399
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:12,580
Wait a minute.

400
00:24:12,580 --> 00:24:15,480
This could be our chance to make a fortune.

401
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:16,520
Next time:

402
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:18,400
Komachi hits it big!

403
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,240
I'm counting on you.

